{"id":"79d9355f-2351-485f-947d-6c9e78f30bbf","object":"chat.completion","created":1784983064,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    core_distance = case['core_distance']\\n    distances = case['distances']\\n    \\n    # Validate nodes and core_distance\\n    if not nodes:\\n        raise ValueError('No nodes')\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        if n not in core_distance:\\n            raise ValueError(f'Missing core_distance for node {n}')\\n    \\n    # Build distance lookup for unordered pairs (sorted tuple)\\n    dist_dict = {}\\n    for entry in distances:\\n        if len(entry) != 3:\\n            raise ValueError('Invalid distance entry')\\n        u, v, d = entry\\n        key = tuple(sorted((u, v)))\\n        if key in dist_dict:\\n            raise ValueError('Duplicate distance entry')\\n        dist_dict[key] = d\\n    \\n    # Sort nodes for deterministic indexing\\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes)\\n    node_to_idx = {n: i for i, n in enumerate(sorted_nodes)}\\n    n = len(sorted_nodes)\\n    \\n    # Generate all candidate edges with mutual reachability\\n    edges = []\\n    for i in range(n):\\n        for j in range(i+1, n):\\n            u = sorted_nodes[i]\\n            v = sorted_nodes[j]\\n            key = (u, v)\\n            if key not in dist_dict:\\n                continue  # missing distance -> no edge\\n            d = dist_dict[key]\\n            mr = max(core_distance[u], core_distance[v], d)\\n            edges.append((mr, u, v))\\n    \\n    # Sort by mutual reachability, then by node IDs (lexicographic)\\n    edges.sort(key=lambda x: (x[0], x[1], x[2]))\\n    \\n    # Union-Find\\n    parent = list(range(n))\\n    rank = [0]*n\\n    \\n    def find(x):\\n        while parent[x] != x:\\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\\n            x = parent[x]\\n        return x\\n    \\n    def union(x, y):\\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\\n        if rx == ry:\\n            return False\\n        if rank[rx] < rank[ry]:\\n            parent[rx] = ry\\n        elif rank[rx] > rank[ry]:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n        else:\\n            # tie-break by index\\n            if rx < ry:\\n                parent[ry] = rx\\n                rank[rx] += 1\\n            else:\\n                parent[rx] = ry\\n                rank[ry] += 1\\n        return True\\n    \\n    # Kruskal\\n    selected_edges = []\\n    total_weight = 0.0\\n    for w, u, v in edges:\\n        if len(selected_edges) == n-1:\\n            break\\n        if union(node_to_idx[u], node_to_idx[v]):\\n            selected_edges.append([u, v])\\n            total_weight += w\\n    \\n    if n > 1 and len(selected_edges) != n-1:\\n        raise ValueError('Graph is disconnected')\\n    \\n    return {'edges': selected_edges, 'total_weight': total_weight}\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement `solve(case)` that computes a mutual reachability MST given nodes, core_distance dict, and distances list. The input `case` is a payload dict with keys: \"nodes\" (list of node IDs), \"core_distance\" (dict mapping node to float), \"distances\" (list of [node1, node2, distance] triples). We must produce an output with selected edges and total weight.\n\nThe task description says: Compute core distances (already given), mutual-reachability edge weights, and a deterministic minimum spanning tree. The procedure: For each pair, compute mutual reachability as max(core_left, core_right, distance). Then canonicalize undirected endpoints (sort node IDs). Sort by reachability then endpoint IDs. Run Kruskal with deterministic union-find until n-1 edges selected. Reject disconnected inputs (i.e., if we can't form a spanning tree). Return selected edges plus total weight.\n\nWe need to handle tie-breaking: sort by (mutual_reachability, node1, node2) where node1 < node2 lexicographically (string comparison). For 